# Qdrant — Best Practices

<!-- cs: Best practices pro Qdrant vektorovou databázi -->

## Docker Setup

<!-- cs: Docker setup -->

```yaml
# docker-compose.yml — infrastructure section
services:
  qdrant:
    image: qdrant/qdrant:v1.9.2        # always pin the version
    ports:
      - "6333:6333"                     # REST API
      - "6334:6334"                     # gRPC
    volumes:
      - qdrant_data:/qdrant/storage
    environment:
      QDRANT__TELEMETRY_DISABLED: "true"
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "curl", "-f", "http://localhost:6333/healthz"]
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 5

volumes:
  qdrant_data:
```

## Python Client Setup

<!-- cs: Python klient -->

```python
# Use grpc for production (faster batch operations); http for dev/scripts
from qdrant_client import QdrantClient
from qdrant_client.models import Distance, VectorParams

# ✅ async client — preferred for FastAPI / async services
from qdrant_client import AsyncQdrantClient

client = AsyncQdrantClient(host="localhost", port=6334, prefer_grpc=True)

# ✅ sync client — for scripts and migrations
client = QdrantClient(url="http://localhost:6333")
```

## Collection Design

<!-- cs: Návrh kolekcí -->

```python
from qdrant_client.models import Distance, VectorParams, HnswConfigDiff

# ✅ Create collection — idempotent (recreate_collection replaces existing)
await client.recreate_collection(
    collection_name="documents",
    vectors_config=VectorParams(
        size=1536,              # must match embedding model output dimension
        distance=Distance.COSINE,
    ),
    hnsw_config=HnswConfigDiff(
        m=16,                   # higher → better recall, more memory
        ef_construct=200,       # higher → better index quality, slower indexing
    ),
    on_disk_payload=True,       # ✅ keep payload on disk — saves RAM for large corpora
)

# ✅ Named vectors — for multi-vector (e.g. title + body) search
await client.recreate_collection(
    collection_name="articles",
    vectors_config={
        "title": VectorParams(size=1536, distance=Distance.COSINE),
        "body":  VectorParams(size=1536, distance=Distance.COSINE),
    },
)
```

## Payload Indexing

<!-- cs: Indexování payloadu -->

Always index fields used in `filter` — without index, filter scans all vectors:
<!-- cs: Vždy indexuj pole používaná ve filter — bez indexu probíhá full scan. -->

```python
from qdrant_client.models import PayloadSchemaType

# Run once after collection creation (idempotent)
await client.create_payload_index(
    collection_name="documents",
    field_name="source_id",
    field_schema=PayloadSchemaType.KEYWORD,
)
await client.create_payload_index(
    collection_name="documents",
    field_name="created_at",
    field_schema=PayloadSchemaType.DATETIME,
)
```

## Point Upsert

<!-- cs: Vkládání bodů -->

```python
from qdrant_client.models import PointStruct
import uuid

# ✅ Use UUID for point IDs — consistent with PostgreSQL PK convention
await client.upsert(
    collection_name="documents",
    points=[
        PointStruct(
            id=str(uuid.uuid4()),          # or deterministic: uuid5(NAMESPACE, source_id)
            vector=embedding,              # List[float], length must match VectorParams.size
            payload={
                "source_id": doc.source_id,
                "content":   doc.content[:500],  # store snippet, not full text
                "created_at": doc.created_at.isoformat(),
            },
        )
    ],
    wait=True,   # ✅ wait=True ensures point is searchable immediately
)
```

## Search with Filter

<!-- cs: Vyhledávání s filtrem -->

```python
from qdrant_client.models import Filter, FieldCondition, MatchValue, Range

# ✅ Filtered semantic search
results = await client.search(
    collection_name="documents",
    query_vector=query_embedding,
    query_filter=Filter(
        must=[
            FieldCondition(key="source_id", match=MatchValue(value="feed-42")),
        ],
        must_not=[
            FieldCondition(key="is_deleted", match=MatchValue(value=True)),
        ],
    ),
    limit=10,
    with_payload=True,   # ✅ return payload — avoids a second DB lookup
    with_vectors=False,  # ❌ don't return vectors unless you need them (bandwidth)
    score_threshold=0.7, # optional: minimum cosine similarity
)

# Access results
for hit in results:
    print(hit.id, hit.score, hit.payload["content"])
```

## Batch Operations

<!-- cs: Dávkové operace -->

```python
# ✅ Always upsert in batches — individual upserts are slow for bulk loading
BATCH_SIZE = 256

async def upsert_batch(points: list[PointStruct]) -> None:
    for i in range(0, len(points), BATCH_SIZE):
        await client.upsert(
            collection_name="documents",
            points=points[i : i + BATCH_SIZE],
            wait=True,
        )

# ✅ Delete by filter (e.g. clean up outdated source)
await client.delete(
    collection_name="documents",
    points_selector=Filter(
        must=[FieldCondition(key="source_id", match=MatchValue(value="feed-42"))]
    ),
)
```

## Repository Pattern

<!-- cs: Repository pattern -->

```
src/
└── <module>/
    └── vector_repository.py   # all Qdrant calls here — not in business logic
```

- One `VectorRepository` class per collection.
  <!-- cs: Jedna třída VectorRepository na kolekci. -->
- Business logic never calls `qdrant_client` directly — only through the repository.
  <!-- cs: Business logika nevolá qdrant_client přímo — jen přes repository. -->
- Constructor accepts `AsyncQdrantClient` — injectable for testing with `AsyncQdrantClient(":memory:")`.
  <!-- cs: Konstruktor přijímá AsyncQdrantClient — injectovatelný pro testy přes in-memory klient. -->
